35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The scanning contractors slip when big clients book. But the halls kept running despite road closures.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,The bus links are gone in the outer wards. People can't reach us easily.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,The grant only covers fees for a year. Then the flat budget takes over. That is a trap.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The old outreach stops had forty visitors a session. The digitisation project failed, but the evening groups still work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that no one is trained to supervise outside facilitators. Also, remote use peaks after we lock up.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"So, relying on external suppliers is risky. But community-led efforts seem more resilient.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"If we can't reach the outer wards, a mobile service might be the only way.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,I agree with Ryuji. We need a model that doesn't depend on one-off grants.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,The evening groups prove that community coordination works. We should look at that model.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If we hire outside facilitators, we need training. Or we need to use the volunteers we have.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The mobile service could bypass the road closures if it uses different routes or timing.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,Yes! A mobile branch could go to the wards where the buses stopped running.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,But the vehicle running costs overran last year. We need to be careful with that.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,The mobile service is like the outreach stops. It has a track record of high attendance.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I’m worried about the staff workload for a mobile service. Who will drive and manage it?,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We need to weigh the risks. The mobile service has high demand but high operational risk.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I really hope we can make it work for the outer wards.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I will support a proposal that addresses the funding gap and the staffing issue.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I think the mobile service is the strongest candidate based on the data.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m still unsure about the staffing, but I see the need.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
